## Context
Report tables and charts currently read from scattered sources
(all_metrics.json, per-sweep CSVs, raw JSON outputs). After migration,
all reporting must derive from the measurements table.

## Actions
1. Refactor `summarize_sweep.py` to read from measurements table
2. Refactor `tabulate_census.py` to read from measurements table
3. Refactor `plot_pareto.py` to read from measurements table
4. Refactor `plot_census.py` to read from measurements table
5. `runner.py evaluate-all` appends RunRecord rows (not all_metrics.json)

## Exit criteria
- All report tables and charts render correctly from measurements.jsonl
- No code path reads all_metrics.json for reporting
- `make` builds report successfully
